200 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 19 0 R
/E (Chrono Map allows ALL-IN to understand where it is during the performance. The colored markings on the floor work as location tags, and the robot uses its sensors to identify each one. When ALL-IN detects a specific color, it recognizes its position on the stage and uses that information to understand the current part of the journey and decide what action should happen next.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [180]
>>
endobj
201 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 19 0 R
/E (Our communication architecture connects different microcontrollers, robots, scenery elements, and computer applications through BLE broadcasting. It acts as a bridge between technologies, allowing devices with different hardware and programming languages to exchange signals during the performance. Each part responds to specific signals, coordinating robot movements, scenery effects, and screen updates in real time. This shared communication system allows the individual parts to work together, keeping their actions synchronized with the story.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [181]
>>
endobj
