227 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 19 0 R
/E (Our ALL-IN robot uses a precise movement system based on line following with PID control, which helps stabilize its trajectory and improve movement accuracy. The robot is controlled by a LEGO SPIKE Prime running MicroPython. We chose this approach so that, even though ALL-IN is LEGO-based, it can still send and receive BLE signals and communicate with different microcontrollers and peripherals used throughout the project.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [207]
>>
endobj
228 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 19 0 R
/E (The EDGY robot, representing the Ancient Egypt era, has a custom 3D-modeled base and is controlled by a LEGO EV3 running MicroPython. To enable BLE communication, the EV3 is connected to a micro:bit through serial communication. The micro:bit acts as a bridge, receiving and transmitting BLE signals for the EV3. This allows EDGY to remain fully integrated with the performance, being activated only at specific moments of the story.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [208]
>>
endobj
229 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H6
/P 19 0 R
/T (80s - System Architecture)
/E (80s - System Architecture)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [209]
>>
endobj
230 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 19 0 R
/E (The 1980s stage is designed to be colorful, dynamic, and fun. When ALL-IN leaves the Time Machine and enters this era, an ESP32 receives a BLE signal and activates the entire scene. The system turns on gyro-style lights, controls motors that rotate part of the stage background, and activates WS2812B addressable LED strips, creating a bright and energetic atmosphere inspired by the 1980s.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [210]
>>
endobj
231 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 19 0 R
/E (The Time Machine is one of the main elements of our story. It uses an ESP32 to control its LED system, changing the colors according to each era and the current moment of the performance. In addition, depending on the era, the Time Machine also changes the content displayed on the main screen, creating a synchronized connection between the physical scenery, lighting effects, and the story.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [211]
>>
endobj
