<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 19 0 R
/E (Our BLE communication architecture works like a broadcast network: each device can send signals that are received by all connected systems, while each robot or stage element only reacts to the commands intended for it. This allows the entire performance to stay synchronized without requiring direct one-to-one connections between every device.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [225]
>>
endobj
246 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 19 0 R
/E (Our EV3 communication innovation combines EV3Dev/MicroPython, serial communication, and BLE. Because the EV3 does not handle our BLE system directly, a micro:bit works as a bridge, exchanging data with the EV3 through serial while sending and receiving BLE signals from the rest of the project. This allows older EV3 robots to become part of the same modern wireless architecture.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [226]
>>
endobj
